+ **Shot type**: extreme close-up → close-up (slow downward drift)
+ **Subject + action**: A single frog-button knot node fills the frame; the camera drifts downward along the placket edge, revealing silk thread direction, seam finishing, and hand-stitched trim in sequence—each detail held for 1–2 seconds before the drift continues.
+ **Setting**: Stable, diffused directional light (no flicker, no wind); macro or long-focal-length lens to compress depth and isolate texture; background is pure soft neutral tone.
+ **Camera movement**: Extremely slow downward drift (near-static), approximately 1 cm of real subject travel over 6 seconds; no shake, no rack-focus mid-movement.
